// Asset Administration Shell 3.2: the graph model and sample data
//
// Generated by ../../cypher.py from model.json and sample.json. Edit those and regenerate, rather than this file.
//
// The digital twin of a synchronous servo motor, serial number 2407-00381, from Halden Antriebe GmbH, a fictional
// drive maker: an asset administration shell with its asset information and specific asset IDs, and two submodels
// following the IDTA templates, Digital Nameplate and Technical Data. Their elements, among them multi-language
// properties, a list of markings, collections and a range, carry semantic IDs pointing at ECLASS IRDIs, the
// templates' IRIs or the maker's concept descriptions, which define rated torque and degree of protection by IEC
// 61360 data specifications and the newton metre by a unit of measure data specification.
//
// Run it against an empty database of Neo4j 5 or later, Enterprise Edition, for its node key and property existence
// constraints, e.g. with cypher-shell -f model.cypher. It merges every node and relationship, so it can be run again.

